  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Recall that $n$ is an odd number if $n=2k+1$ for some integer $k$. Prove that if $n$ is odd, then $n^2$ is odd.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n^2=2(2k^2+2k)+1$, which is odd because $2k^2+2k$ is an integer.",
      "worked": "Let $n=2k+1$, where $k$ is an integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n^2&=(2k+1)^2\\\\n^2&=4k^2+4k+1\\\\n^2&=2(2k^2+2k)+1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $2k^2+2k$ is an integer, $n^2$ has the form twice an integer plus one. Therefore, $n^2$ is odd.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
